 [{:id "BIP-019-SOAK-F2"
   :severity :medium
   :title "Periodic 4-5 epoch (6-8 s) Streamlet finalization sawtooth every 6 epochs after a validator restarts"
   :observed "Phase A (ep 0 -> 120) had 0 stalls and maxGap=2 (120/120 blocks finalized). Immediately after Phase B (SIGKILL + restart of node1 from fin=79), 1-2 leader slots per 6-epoch cycle went un-notarized permanently through ep 347 (node2/node3/ns1 finalized 291 blocks across 347 epochs; 52 epochs skipped between ep 144 and ep 347). Because Streamlet requires 3 consecutive notarized epochs to finalize, each skipped leader slot produced a deterministic 4-5 epoch (6.0-8.1 s) finalization pause every 6 epochs (25 intervals > 3 epochs across Phases B/C/D, max gap = 5 epochs) before jumping +5 epochs in one step."
   :distinction-from-f1 "Unlike BIP-019-SOAK-F1 (107-epoch / ~97 s stall, now 100% resolved by e6194fb), this is bounded to 4-5 epochs (~6-8 s), never exceeds gap=5, keeps settled gap=1 and skew=0, and never triggers corrupt-block-depth-repaired."
   :recommended-followup "Investigate why a restarted validator's leader slot fails to collect a notarization quorum on every subsequent 6-epoch rotation (check whether :tick-suppressed-epoch-already-advanced min-dwell suppression or post-snapshot block-depth/parent-hash divergence causes the restarted leader's proposal to be missed or rejected by peers)."}]}
